<title>UK: Novorossiisk reopens after 33 hour closure - shipper.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk reopens after 33 hour closure - shipper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's main crude export port of Novorossiisk in the Black Sea reopened on Monday morning after 33 hours' closure, a shipping inspector said.</p>
<p>The port closed on Saturday night at 2115 local time due to high winds, but reopened at 0600 local time this morning when the wind subsided to force 4-5.</p>
<p>Novorossiisk last shut on Friday, but reopened for a short time before closing again on Saturday night.</p>
<p>The inspector said Ventspils, Odessa and Tuapse were all open on Monday.</p>
